  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dakota Ridge’s name comes from the Dakota Sioux word for “friend” or “ally,” paired with the word “ridge” that describes its prominent hilltop setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/dakota-ridge-15440",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits atop the Dakota Hogback, a sharp ridge that runs north‑south and is also known locally as Dinosaur Ridge near Morrison.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dakota_Ridge%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Just 17 miles southwest of downtown Denver, Dakota Ridge offers sweeping views of the Rocky Mountains while remaining a quiet residential enclave.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dakota_Ridge%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A short drive from Dakota Ridge leads to Dinosaur Ridge, a National Historic Landmark where visitors can see hundreds of preserved dinosaur footprints.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.islands.com/2031745/dakota-ridge-littleton-colorado-suburb-scenic-rocky-mountain-views-denver-proximity/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area is home to historic mining relics, including the Santiago Mill, and memorials such as the Griffin Monument, both reflecting early Colorado frontier life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.islands.com/2031745/dakota-ridge-littleton-colorado-suburb-scenic-rocky-mountain-views-denver-proximity/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Dakota Ridge was once considered for incorporation in 1988, but voters rejected the proposal, keeping the community as a census‑designated place within Jefferson County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
